// strapd's Niri defaults.
//
// Loaded by ~/.config/niri/config.kdl, which loads its own files after this
// one, niri includes are positional, so anything set here can be overridden
// there. Nothing in this tree is yours to edit; a package update replaces it.
//
// Split one file per subject, so
// that overriding one thing has an obvious file to read first.
//
// The session environment is not among them: it is the same for all three
// compositors, so it lives in default/uwsm/env.d/10-strapd, which uwsm
// sources before starting any of them.

include "input.kdl"
include "looknfeel.kdl"
include "windows.kdl"
include "autostart.kdl"
